{
  "components": {
    "schemas": {
      "AnswerRequest": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "An answer to a pending clarifying question.\n\nOne field. Note the three that are absent and will not be added: no ``sessionOwner``, because\nthe answerer comes from trusted identity; no ``confirm``, because an affirmative answer is not\nconsent; and no ``workItemId``, because an answer does not target a decision.\n\n``content`` is bounded at :data:`~ragcore.graph.nodes.clarification_interrupt.\nMAX_ANSWER_CHARACTERS`. The answer becomes part of the next prompt, and an unbounded answer is\nan unbounded model call metered against the organisation.",
        "properties": {
          "content": {
            "default": "",
            "title": "Content",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "title": "AnswerRequest",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "ConsentRequest": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "A consent decision — **the only way consent is ever recorded**.\n\nOne field, an enum of two. Deliberately not a boolean: ``consent(True)`` says nothing at a\ncall site, and .claude/rules/10-principles.md P-20 prohibits a boolean flag that\nhides behaviour.",
        "properties": {
          "verdict": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ConsentVerdict"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "verdict"
        ],
        "title": "ConsentRequest",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "ConsentVerdict": {
        "description": "An end user's decision on an operation affecting their own account or device.\n\nTwo members, mirroring ``data-model.md`` ``consent.verdict`` and the two consent trigger kinds.\nA boolean would collapse this to ``True``/``False`` at every call site, which the baseline\nprohibits as \"a boolean parameter flag that hides behaviour\"\n(.claude/rules/10-principles.md P-20).",
        "enum": [
          "granted",
          "refused"
        ],
        "title": "ConsentVerdict",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "ExecutionResultRequest": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "An execution result posted by the desktop client.\n\n**A client-reported result is a claim, not proof** (ADR-0004). It becomes a\n``client_attested`` verification outcome and MUST NOT be reported to a user or written to the\nsystem of record as confirmed resolution.",
        "properties": {
          "detail": {
            "default": "",
            "title": "Detail",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "exitStatus": {
            "title": "Exitstatus",
            "type": "integer"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "exitStatus"
        ],
        "title": "ExecutionResultRequest",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "FeedbackRequest": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "A quality signal against one agent-authored message.\n\nOne field, an enum of two. Deliberately not a boolean — ``feedback(True)`` says nothing at a\ncall site — and deliberately without a comment field; see the module docstring.\n\n**Feedback never influences authorization, governance treatment, retrieval scope or\nexecution** (spec FR-SESS-013). It is read by reporting and by nothing else.",
        "properties": {
          "signal": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FeedbackSignal"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "signal"
        ],
        "title": "FeedbackRequest",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "FeedbackSignal": {
        "description": "A per-message thumbs signal (spec FR-SESS-009).\n\n**Never an input to a decision.** Governance, retrieval and execution MUST NOT read it\n(spec FR-SESS-011a, ``data-model.md`` §Feedback). It is a quality signal, and the reason it\nlives here rather than beside the treatment enums is to keep that separation legible.",
        "enum": [
          "positive",
          "negative"
        ],
        "title": "FeedbackSignal",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "NegotiateResponse": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "Where to connect, and on what.\n\nCarries no tenant, no role and no approval state. It names an endpoint and a group — both of\nwhich the platform chose — and nothing a client could act on as authority.",
        "properties": {
          "group": {
            "title": "Group",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "url": {
            "title": "Url",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "url",
          "group"
        ],
        "title": "NegotiateResponse",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "ProblemDetails": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "The RFC 9457 error body, declared so it appears in every emitted document.\n\n**The document has to say what an error looks like, or the contract is only half emitted.**\n:mod:`ragcore.api.middleware.problems` already returns this shape at runtime; without a model\nthe generator falls back to FastAPI's ``HTTPValidationError``, and the published contract then\ndescribes an error body the service never sends.\n\nMirrors ``Synthia.Contracts.Errors.ProblemContract`` on the .NET side field for field, because a\nclient calls both deployables and must parse one error contract, not two.\n\n``correlationId`` is the one addition to RFC 9457, and it is what lets a user quoting an error\nbe followed across an asynchronous, suspendable flow (spec FR-OPS-001).",
        "properties": {
          "correlationId": {
            "title": "Correlationid",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "detail": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Detail"
          },
          "instance": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Instance"
          },
          "status": {
            "title": "Status",
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "title": {
            "title": "Title",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": {
            "title": "Type",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "type",
          "title",
          "status",
          "correlationId"
        ],
        "title": "ProblemDetails",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "SendMessageRequest": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "One turn of conversation.\n\n**Chat text cannot grant authority** (spec FR-IDENT-004). An affirmative message is never\nconsent — only ``POST /work/{id}/consent`` records that — so there is no ``confirm`` field here\nfor a client to set, and nothing downstream reads ``content`` to decide anything.",
        "properties": {
          "content": {
            "title": "Content",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "content"
        ],
        "title": "SendMessageRequest",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "StartSessionResponse": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "The identifier of a newly started session.",
        "properties": {
          "sessionId": {
            "format": "uuid",
            "title": "Sessionid",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "sessionId"
        ],
        "title": "StartSessionResponse",
        "type": "object"
      }
    }
  },
  "info": {
    "description": "The customer audience. Generated from the running service; not hand-maintained. Identity is derived at the gateway and no operation accepts a tenant, role or audience parameter.",
    "title": "Synthia Customer API",
    "version": "v1"
  },
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "paths": {
    "/api/customer/v1/messages/{messageId}/feedback": {
      "delete": {
        "description": "Withdraw a previously recorded signal.\n\nIdempotent: withdrawing when nothing is recorded succeeds, because the caller's intent holds\neither way and a 404 would send a client into a retry loop over a state it has reached.\n\nReturns:\n    204 when no signal from this caller remains on the message. 404 when the message is not\n    theirs.",
        "operationId": "withdraw_feedback_api_customer_v1_messages__messageId__feedback_delete",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "description": "An agent-authored message.",
            "in": "path",
            "name": "messageId",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "description": "An agent-authored message.",
              "format": "uuid",
              "title": "Messageid",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "204": {
            "description": "No signal from this caller remains."
          },
          "401": {
            "content": {
              "application/problem+json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProblemDetails"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Unauthenticated"
          },
          "403": {
            "content": {
              "application/problem+json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProblemDetails"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Not authorized"
          },
          "404": {
            "content": {
              "application/problem+json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProblemDetails"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Not found"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/problem+json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProblemDetails"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Invalid request"
          },
          "500": {
            "content": {
              "application/problem+json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProblemDetails"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Internal error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Withdraw Feedback",
        "tags": [
          "customer"
        ]
      },
      "put": {
        "description": "Record or revise a thumbs signal.\n\n``PUT`` because feedback is revisable: repeating it replaces the previous signal rather than\ncreating a second.\n\nReturns:\n    204 on success — there is no body, because there is nothing to return that the client did\n    not just send, and an echoed signal is a second source of truth for a value the client\n    already holds.\n\nRaises:\n    HTTPException: Never raised here. A message that is not an agent-authored message in the\n        caller's own session is reported as **404** through the problem contract, because\n        existence is tenant-scoped information.",
        "operationId": "record_feedback_api_customer_v1_messages__messageId__feedback_put",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "description": "An agent-authored message.",
            "in": "path",
            "name": "messageId",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "description": "An agent-authored message.",
              "format": "uuid",
              "title": "Messageid",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FeedbackRequest"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "204": {
            "description": "The signal was recorded or replaced."
          },
          "401": {
            "content": {
              "application/problem+json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProblemDetails"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Unauthenticated"
          },
          "403": {
            "content": {
              "application/problem+json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProblemDetails"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Not authorized"
          },
          "404": {
            "content": {
